<title>USA: TABLE - Jackpot Enterprises Q4 net income rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Jackpot Enterprises Q4 net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>LAS VEGAS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jackpot Enterprises Inc</p>
<p>				  Three Months Ended  12 Months Ended</p>
<p>					  June 30,	    June 30,</p>
<p>				    1997	   1996    1997    1996</p>
<p> Revenues Totals	     24,442	23,077  91,904  91,108</p>
<p>Operating income before</p>
<p>write-down of casino</p>
<p>  properties		    3,106	 2,386   9,822   9,341</p>
<p>Loss from write-down</p>
<p>  of casino properties	   --	 2,247	--   2,247</p>
<p> Operating income	     3,106	   139   9,822   7,094</p>
<p> Net income		     2,362	   340   7,844   5,855</p>
<p> Earnings per common share    .26	   .04     .85     .63</p>
<p>Weighted average number</p>
<p>  of common shares	    9,086	 9,317   9,237   9,307</p>
<p>(Dollars and shares in thousands, except per-share data)</p>
<p>NOTE:  -- Company says net income and earnings per share for fiscal 1998 will be adversely affected compared to fiscal 1997 due to the intensely competitive market conditions prevailing for gaming machinte route operators and as a result of the loss of a significant chain store customer on June 30, 1997, which accounted for approximately 6 percent of total revenues and a significant amount of operating income in fiscal 1997, and to significant increases in location rent effective July 1 in connection with long-term contract renewals with four of Jackpot's largest chain store customers.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk 212 859-1700))</p>
</text>
